    {
      "index": 4,
      "question": "What insurance must a vendor carry to be onboarded?",
      "status": 200,
      "answer": "To be onboarded, a vendor must carry commercial general liability insurance of at least 1,000,000 USD per occurrence and 2,000,000 USD aggregate \u2014 with life-safety and roofing vendors required to show 2,000,000 USD per occurrence \u2014 plus workers compensation coverage as required by the vendor's state, or a valid exemption [1]. The certificate of insurance must be provided before a purchase order is issued, and it is re-verified 30 days before it expires, with an expired certificate suspending the vendor from new work [1].",
